window.META_MATH = {"subject": "Advanced Calculus", "projects": [{"id": "AC-01", "slug": "mean-value-theorem", "title": "Mean Value Theorem", "target": "<p>If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><mo>→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f:[a,b]\\to\\mathbb R</annotation></semantics></math>\nis continuous on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">[a,b]</annotation></semantics></math>\nand differentiable on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(a,b)</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a&lt;b</annotation></semantics></math>,\nprove there is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">c\\in(a,b)</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f&#39;(c)=(f(b)-f(a))/(b-a)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "imports": ["<p>Import the extreme value theorem for continuous real functions on a\nclosed bounded interval. Fermat’s stationary-point lemma is proved below\nby one-sided difference quotients. Differentiability is required only in\nthe open interval.</p>"], "nodes": [{"id": "N1", "title": "Rolle’s theorem", "proof": "1. The extreme value theorem gives a maximum and a minimum.\n\n2. If h is constant, h′=0 at every interior point.\n\n3. Otherwise at least one extremal value differs from the common endpoint value, so an extremizer c lies inside(a,b).\n\n4. At an interior local maximum, difference quotients with positive step are≤0 and with negative step are≥0.\n\n5. If the two-sided derivative exists it is therefore0.\n\n6. At a minimum the inequalities reverse and give the same conclusion.\n\n7. Thus Rolle’s theorem holds.", "role": "<p>Find an interior extremum unless the function is constant.</p>", "inputs": "<p>Continuous h with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h(a)=h(b)</annotation></semantics></math>,\ndifferentiable inside; foundational imports stated in §1</p>", "export": "<p>An interior point with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h&#39;(c)=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E1/v1: An interior point with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h&#39;(c)=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Retain Continuous h with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h(a)=h(b)</annotation></semantics></math>,\ndifferentiable inside; foundational imports stated in §1; keep their\nassumptions and versions attached.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Find an interior extremum unless the function is constant.</p>", "Sense": "<p>A corner at an extremizer prevents the derivative conclusion.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E1/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "activities": ["<p>The extreme value theorem gives a maximum and a minimum.</p>", "<p>If h is constant,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h&#39;=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nat every interior point.</p>", "<p>Otherwise at least one extremal value differs from the common\nendpoint value, so an extremizer c lies inside (a,b).</p>", "<p>At an interior local maximum, difference quotients with positive step\nare\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\le 0</annotation></semantics></math>\nand with negative step are\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\ge 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>If the two-sided derivative exists it is therefore 0.</p>", "<p>At a minimum the inequalities reverse and give the same\nconclusion.</p>", "<p>Thus Rolle’s theorem holds.</p>"], "exportId": "E1", "gate": "<p>A corner at an extremizer prevents the derivative conclusion. Publish\nonly after checking every displayed deduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N1: A corner at an extremizer prevents the\nderivative conclusion. Recheck dependent nodes N2.</p>"}, {"id": "N2", "title": "Subtract the secant", "proof": "1. Set m=(f(b)−f(a))/(b−a) and h(x)=f(x)−f(a)−m(x−a).\n\n2. It has the required regularity and h(a)=h(b)=0.\n\n3. By Rolle there is c∈(a,b) with h′(c)=f′(c)−m=0.\n\n4. Hence f′(c)=m, exactly the mean value theorem.\n\n5. No differentiability at the endpoints was needed.", "role": "<p>Make endpoints equal by an auxiliary affine function.</p>", "inputs": "<p>Given f and interval\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a&lt;b</annotation></semantics></math>;\nprior exports E1/v1</p>", "export": "<p>The specified secant slope is attained by an interior derivative.</p>", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E2/v1: The specified secant slope is attained by an interior\nderivative.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Retain Given f and interval\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a&lt;b</annotation></semantics></math>;\nprior exports E1/v1; keep their assumptions and versions attached.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Make endpoints equal by an auxiliary affine function.</p>", "Sense": "<p>Division by\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">b-a</annotation></semantics></math>\nis valid because\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a&lt;b</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E2/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "activities": ["<p>Set\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m=(f(b)-f(a))/(b-a)</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h(x)=f(x)-f(a)-m(x-a)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>It has the required regularity and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h(a)=h(b)=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>By Rolle there is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">c\\in (a,b)</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h&#39;(c)=f&#39;(c)-m=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Hence\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f&#39;(c)=m</annotation></semantics></math>,\nexactly the mean value theorem.</p>", "<p>No differentiability at the endpoints was needed.</p>"], "exportId": "E2", "gate": "<p>Division by\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">b-a</annotation></semantics></math>\nis valid because\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a&lt;b</annotation></semantics></math>.\nPublish only after checking every displayed deduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N2: Division by\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">b-a</annotation></semantics></math>\nis valid because\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a&lt;b</annotation></semantics></math>.\nWithhold this terminal result until its gate passes.</p>"}], "edges": [{"source": "N1", "target": "N2", "export": "E1/v1", "id": "T1", "activity": "N2: Subtract the secant", "gate": "<p>Use the same mathematical objects and hypotheses as the source\nexport. Receiving contract: Given f and interval\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a&lt;b</annotation></semantics></math>;\nprior exports E1/v1</p>"}], "proof": "<p>Read these steps in order as one proof; the diagram is optional.\nNumbered activities identify the specific constructions and deductions\nowned by each node.</p>\n<h3 id=\"n1-rolles-theorem-1\">§4.N1 — Rolle’s theorem</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p>The extreme value theorem gives a maximum and a minimum.</p></li>\n<li><p>If h is constant,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h&#39;=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nat every interior point.</p></li>\n<li><p>Otherwise at least one extremal value differs from the common\nendpoint value, so an extremizer c lies inside (a,b).</p></li>\n<li><p>At an interior local maximum, difference quotients with positive\nstep are\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\le 0</annotation></semantics></math>\nand with negative step are\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\ge 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>If the two-sided derivative exists it is therefore 0.</p></li>\n<li><p>At a minimum the inequalities reverse and give the same\nconclusion.</p></li>\n<li><p>Thus Rolle’s theorem holds.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"n2-subtract-the-secant-1\">§4.N2 — Subtract the secant</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p>Set\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m=(f(b)-f(a))/(b-a)</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h(x)=f(x)-f(a)-m(x-a)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>It has the required regularity and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h(a)=h(b)=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>By Rolle there is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">c\\in (a,b)</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h&#39;(c)=f&#39;(c)-m=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>Hence\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f&#39;(c)=m</annotation></semantics></math>,\nexactly the mean value theorem.</p></li>\n<li><p>No differentiability at the endpoints was needed.</p></li>\n</ol>", "example": "<p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(x)=x^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>\non[1,3], the secant slope is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(9-1)/2=4</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe derivative 2x equals 4 at\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">c=2</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe auxiliary\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h=x^{2}-1-4(x-1)</annotation></semantics></math>\nhas its interior minimum there.</p>", "boundary": ["<p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(x)=|x|</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">on[-1,1]</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthe secant slope is 0 but its derivative where defined is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>±</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\pm 1</annotation></semantics></math>.\nSense detects the absent differentiability at 0, exactly where Rolle’s\nextremum argument would require it.</p>"], "repair": [{"label": "Failure and correction", "html": "<p>This is an authored teaching trace, not a recorded agent run.</p>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Ego\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math>\nMemory:</strong> register the §1 theorem, imports, and requested exports\nbefore beginning the proof.</li>\n<li><strong>Intellect\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math>\nAction:</strong> choose the bridges in §3 and carry out the numbered\nactivities in §4; transmit only established E-exports along the §2\nDAG.</li>\n<li><strong>Sense\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math>\nresponsible node:</strong> test the specific boundary/failure in §5 and\nthe node’s individual audit. A failing candidate is withheld; downstream\nnodes may not use it.</li>\n<li><strong>Memory + Intellect:</strong> identify whether the error is\nan omitted condition, an invalid inference, or an attempted extension\nbeyond the theorem. Restore the exact contract or explicitly state a\ndifferent one.</li>\n<li><strong>Action:</strong> redo the affected mathematical activity\nusing the repaired condition or inference. Recheck consuming nodes,\nrather than feeding their conclusions back as premises.</li>\n<li><strong>Ego:</strong> publish only the supported export with its\nassumptions and proof location. A hypothetical revised export is v2; the\nwritten proof here is the v1 exposition, not a claim that this repair\nwas executed.</li>\n</ol>"}, {"label": "Hypothesis boundary", "html": "<p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(x)=|x|</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">on[-1,1]</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthe secant slope is 0 but its derivative where defined is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>±</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\pm 1</annotation></semantics></math>.\nSense detects the absent differentiability at 0, exactly where Rolle’s\nextremum argument would require it.</p>"}, {"label": "Version and recheck", "html": "<p>Treat any changed assumption as a new contract. Recheck the revised\nexport and all of its descendants. A backward diagnostic never\nestablishes an earlier theorem. This is an authored teaching trace, not\nan execution log.</p>"}], "standard": true, "sha256": "f6d01b83b1e7671a0e0861f792cc08f7e5aeb3b50b07aaf02b7c2972f6b7a11c", "idea": "<p>A complete authored walkthrough of mean value theorem, with explicit\nmathematical contracts, local verification gates, and reusable\nexports.</p>", "references": "", "pdf": "reports/pdf/mean-value-theorem.pdf"}, {"id": "AC-02", "slug": "fundamental-theorem-of-calculus", "title": "Fundamental Theorem of Calculus", "target": "<p>For continuous\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><mo>→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f:[a,b]\\to\\mathbb R</annotation></semantics></math>,\nprove\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi></msubsup><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F(x)=\\int_a^x f(t)\\,dt</annotation></semantics></math>\nis differentiable on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(a,b)</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F&#39;=f</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIf\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G&#39;=f</annotation></semantics></math>\nthere and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G</annotation></semantics></math>\nis continuous on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">[a,b]</annotation></semantics></math>,\nprove\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\int_a^b f=G(b)-G(a)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "imports": ["<p>Use Riemann integrability of continuous functions on[a,b], additivity\nand integral bounds, and AC-01. An integral with reversed endpoints\nchanges sign. Derivatives of accumulated integrals are taken on (a,b),\nwith one-sided endpoint continuity.</p>"], "nodes": [{"id": "N1", "title": "Differentiate the accumulated integral", "proof": "1. For x interior and sufficiently small nonzero h, additivity gives(F(x+h)−F(x))/h=(1/h)∫_x^{x+h}f(t)dt.\n\n2. Subtract f(x); the absolute difference is bounded by sup between x andx+h of|f(t)−f(x)|, including h<0 using reversed integration.\n\n3. Continuity makes this bound tend to 0.\n\n4. Thus F′(x)=f(x).\n\n5. A global bound on|f| also gives|F(x)−F(y)|≤M|x−y|, so F is continuous through the endpoints.", "role": "<p>Estimate the difference between a local average and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(x)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "inputs": "<p>Continuous f;\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F(x)=\\int _a^x</annotation></semantics></math>\nf; foundational imports stated in §1</p>", "export": "<p>F is continuous on[a,b] and differentiable inside with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F&#39;=f</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E1/v1: F is continuous on[a,b] and differentiable inside with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F&#39;=f</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Retain Continuous f;\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F(x)=\\int _a^x</annotation></semantics></math>\nf; foundational imports stated in §1; keep their assumptions and\nversions attached.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Estimate the difference between a local average and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(x)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Sense": "<p>For negative h, the reversed interval must be treated\nconsistently.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E1/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "activities": ["<p>For x interior and sufficiently small nonzero h, additivity gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msubsup><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(F(x+h)-F(x))/h=(1/h)\\int _x^{x+h}f(t)dt</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Subtract\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(x)</annotation></semantics></math>;\nthe absolute difference is bounded by sup between x andx+h\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">of|f(t)-f(x)|</annotation></semantics></math>,\nincluding\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>\nusing reversed integration.</p>", "<p>Continuity makes this bound tend to 0.</p>", "<p>Thus\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F&#39;(x)=f(x)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>A global bound on|f| also\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>v</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">gives|F(x)-F(y)|\\le M|x-y|</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso F is continuous through the endpoints.</p>"], "exportId": "E1", "gate": "<p>For negative h, the reversed interval must be treated consistently.\nPublish only after checking every displayed deduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N1: For negative h, the reversed interval\nmust be treated consistently. Recheck dependent nodes N2.</p>"}, {"id": "N2", "title": "Compare any antiderivative", "proof": "1. Let H=G−F.\n\n2. It is continuous on[a,b] and H′=0 inside.\n\n3. For any u<v in[a,b], AC-01 yields H(v)−H(u)=H′(c)(v−u)=0.\n\n4. Thus H is constant.\n\n5. Since F(a)=0 and F(b)=∫_a^b f, subtract endpoint values to obtain G(b)−G(a)=F(b)−F(a)=∫_a^b f.\n\n6. This closes the accumulation and antiderivative directions.", "role": "<p>Use the mean value theorem on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G-F</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "inputs": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G&#39;=f</annotation></semantics></math>\ninside and G continuous on[a,b]; prior exports E1/v1</p>", "export": "<p>The two asserted parts of the continuous-integrand FTC.</p>", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E2/v1: The two asserted parts of the continuous-integrand\nFTC.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Retain\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G&#39;=f</annotation></semantics></math>\ninside and G continuous on[a,b]; prior exports E1/v1; keep their\nassumptions and versions attached.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Use the mean value theorem on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G-F</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Sense": "<p>An antiderivative must be continuous at the stated endpoints.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E2/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "activities": ["<p>Let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H=G-F</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>It is continuous on[a,b] and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H&#39;=0</annotation></semantics></math>\ninside.</p>", "<p>For any\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">u&lt;v</annotation></semantics></math>\nin[a,b], AC-01 yields\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H(v)-H(u)=H&#39;(c)(v-u)=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Thus H is constant.</p>", "<p>Since\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F(a)=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F(b)=\\int _a^b</annotation></semantics></math>\nf, subtract endpoint values to obtain\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G(b)-G(a)=F(b)-F(a)=\\int _a^b</annotation></semantics></math>\nf.</p>", "<p>This closes the accumulation and antiderivative directions.</p>"], "exportId": "E2", "gate": "<p>An antiderivative must be continuous at the stated endpoints. Publish\nonly after checking every displayed deduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N2: An antiderivative must be continuous\nat the stated endpoints. Withhold this terminal result until its gate\npasses.</p>"}], "edges": [{"source": "N1", "target": "N2", "export": "E1/v1", "id": "T1", "activity": "N2: Compare any antiderivative", "gate": "<p>Use the same mathematical objects and hypotheses as the source\nexport. Receiving contract:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G&#39;=f</annotation></semantics></math>\ninside and G continuous on[a,b]; prior exports E1/v1</p>"}], "proof": "<p>Read these steps in order as one proof; the diagram is optional.\nNumbered activities identify the specific constructions and deductions\nowned by each node.</p>\n<h3 id=\"n1-differentiate-the-accumulated-integral-1\">§4.N1 —\nDifferentiate the accumulated integral</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p>For x interior and sufficiently small nonzero h, additivity gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msubsup><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(F(x+h)-F(x))/h=(1/h)\\int _x^{x+h}f(t)dt</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>Subtract\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(x)</annotation></semantics></math>;\nthe absolute difference is bounded by sup between x andx+h\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">of|f(t)-f(x)|</annotation></semantics></math>,\nincluding\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>\nusing reversed integration.</p></li>\n<li><p>Continuity makes this bound tend to 0.</p></li>\n<li><p>Thus\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F&#39;(x)=f(x)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>A global bound on|f| also\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>v</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">gives|F(x)-F(y)|\\le M|x-y|</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso F is continuous through the endpoints.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"n2-compare-any-antiderivative-1\">§4.N2 — Compare any\nantiderivative</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p>Let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H=G-F</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>It is continuous on[a,b] and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H&#39;=0</annotation></semantics></math>\ninside.</p></li>\n<li><p>For any\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">u&lt;v</annotation></semantics></math>\nin[a,b], AC-01 yields\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H(v)-H(u)=H&#39;(c)(v-u)=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>Thus H is constant.</p></li>\n<li><p>Since\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F(a)=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F(b)=\\int _a^b</annotation></semantics></math>\nf, subtract endpoint values to obtain\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G(b)-G(a)=F(b)-F(a)=\\int _a^b</annotation></semantics></math>\nf.</p></li>\n<li><p>This closes the accumulation and antiderivative\ndirections.</p></li>\n</ol>", "example": "<p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(t)=3t^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>\non[0,2],\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F(x)=x^{3}</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G(x)=x^{3}+7</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThen\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G(2)-G(0)=8=\\int _{0}^{2}3t^{2}dt</annotation></semantics></math>,\nwhile\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F&#39;=3x^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>\ndemonstrates the local-average limit.</p>", "boundary": ["<p>A discontinuous integrand may be Riemann integrable without\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F&#39;=f</annotation></semantics></math>\nat every point: take\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nexcept\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(0)=1</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">on[-1,1]</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIts accumulated integral is 0, whose derivative at 0 is 0. Sense retains\ncontinuity for this pointwise FTC version.</p>"], "repair": [{"label": "Failure and correction", "html": "<p>This is an authored teaching trace, not a recorded agent run.</p>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Ego\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math>\nMemory:</strong> register the §1 theorem, imports, and requested exports\nbefore beginning the proof.</li>\n<li><strong>Intellect\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math>\nAction:</strong> choose the bridges in §3 and carry out the numbered\nactivities in §4; transmit only established E-exports along the §2\nDAG.</li>\n<li><strong>Sense\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math>\nresponsible node:</strong> test the specific boundary/failure in §5 and\nthe node’s individual audit. A failing candidate is withheld; downstream\nnodes may not use it.</li>\n<li><strong>Memory + Intellect:</strong> identify whether the error is\nan omitted condition, an invalid inference, or an attempted extension\nbeyond the theorem. Restore the exact contract or explicitly state a\ndifferent one.</li>\n<li><strong>Action:</strong> redo the affected mathematical activity\nusing the repaired condition or inference. Recheck consuming nodes,\nrather than feeding their conclusions back as premises.</li>\n<li><strong>Ego:</strong> publish only the supported export with its\nassumptions and proof location. A hypothetical revised export is v2; the\nwritten proof here is the v1 exposition, not a claim that this repair\nwas executed.</li>\n</ol>"}, {"label": "Hypothesis boundary", "html": "<p>A discontinuous integrand may be Riemann integrable without\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F&#39;=f</annotation></semantics></math>\nat every point: take\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nexcept\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(0)=1</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">on[-1,1]</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIts accumulated integral is 0, whose derivative at 0 is 0. Sense retains\ncontinuity for this pointwise FTC version.</p>"}, {"label": "Version and recheck", "html": "<p>Treat any changed assumption as a new contract. Recheck the revised\nexport and all of its descendants. A backward diagnostic never\nestablishes an earlier theorem. This is an authored teaching trace, not\nan execution log.</p>"}], "standard": true, "sha256": "7815c11f5c310d73b38d36532266cdf0483444a96e60b1a5bb46dea2dc4a053b", "idea": "<p>A complete authored walkthrough of fundamental theorem of calculus,\nwith explicit mathematical contracts, local verification gates, and\nreusable exports.</p>", "references": "", "pdf": "reports/pdf/fundamental-theorem-of-calculus.pdf"}, {"id": "AC-03", "slug": "multivariable-taylor-theorem", "title": "Multivariable Taylor Theorem", "target": "<p>Let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f:U\\subset\\mathbb R^n\\to\\mathbb R</annotation></semantics></math>\nbe\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C^{k+1}</annotation></semantics></math>,\nwith the segment from\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a</annotation></semantics></math>\nto\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a+h</annotation></semantics></math>\nin\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">U</annotation></semantics></math>.\nProve\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><mi>/</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>!</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>k</mi><mi>!</mi></mrow></mfrac><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>k</mi></msup><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(a+h)=\\sum_{j=0}^k D^jf(a)[h,\\ldots,h]/j!+\\frac1{k!}\\int_0^1(1-t)^kD^{k+1}f(a+th)[h,\\ldots,h]\\,dt</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "imports": ["<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D^j</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(a)</annotation></semantics></math>\ndenotes the symmetric j-linear derivative;\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D^0f=f</annotation></semantics></math>.\nImport the chain rule and AC-02. The segment is contained in open U and\nf is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C^{(k+1)}</annotation></semantics></math>\nnear it, so\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g(t)=f(a+th)</annotation></semantics></math>\nhas the necessary derivatives on a neighborhood of[0,1]. Derive the\none-variable integral remainder below.</p>\n<p>Here\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k\\ge0</annotation></semantics></math>\nis an integer,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">U\\subset\\mathbb R^n</annotation></semantics></math>\nis open, and the entire segment from\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a</annotation></semantics></math>\nto\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a+h</annotation></semantics></math>\nlies in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">U</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>"], "nodes": [{"id": "N1", "title": "Restrict to a line", "proof": "1. Define g(t)=f(a+th).\n\n2. Repeated chain rule along the affine path yields g^(j)(t)=D^jf(a+th)[h,…,h] for 0≤j≤k+1.\n\n3. For j=0 this means the function itself.\n\n4. Compactness of the segment gives a neighborhood on which these restrictions are defined; no global convexity of U is assumed.", "role": "<p>Reduce the multivariable increment to a scalar parameter.</p>", "inputs": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f\\in C^{(k+1)}</annotation></semantics></math>;\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a+th\\in U</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0\\le t\\le 1</annotation></semantics></math>;\nfoundational imports stated in §1</p>", "export": "<p>The directional derivative identities along the entire segment.</p>", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E1/v1: The directional derivative identities along the entire\nsegment.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Retain\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f\\in C^{(k+1)}</annotation></semantics></math>;\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a+th\\in U</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0\\le t\\le 1</annotation></semantics></math>;\nfoundational imports stated in §1; keep their assumptions and versions\nattached.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Reduce the multivariable increment to a scalar parameter.</p>", "Sense": "<p>Endpoint-only domain membership is insufficient if the segment leaves\nU.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E1/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "activities": ["<p>Define\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g(t)=f(a+th)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Repeated chain rule along the affine path yields\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g^{(j)}(t)=D^jf(a+th)[h,\\ldots ,h]</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0\\le j\\le k+1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">j=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nthis means the function itself.</p>", "<p>Compactness of the segment gives a neighborhood on which these\nrestrictions are defined; no global convexity of U is assumed.</p>"], "exportId": "E1", "gate": "<p>Endpoint-only domain membership is insufficient if the segment leaves\nU. Publish only after checking every displayed deduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N1: Endpoint-only domain membership is\ninsufficient if the segment leaves U. Recheck dependent nodes N2,\nN3.</p>"}, {"id": "N2", "title": "One-variable integral remainder", "proof": "1. For k=0, g(1)−g(0)=∫₀¹g′(t)dt by FTC.\n\n2. For k≥1 integrate I_k=(1/k!)∫₀¹(1−t)^k g^(k+1)(t)dt by parts.\n\n3. The upper boundary is 0, the lower boundary contributes−g^(k)(0)/k!, and the remaining integral is I_(k−1).\n\n4. Hence I_k=I_(k−1)−g^(k)(0)/k!.\n\n5. Iterating to I₀=g(1)−g(0) gives g(1)=∑_{j=0}^k g^(j)(0)/j!+I_k.", "role": "<p>Apply FTC and integrate by parts repeatedly.</p>", "inputs": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g\\in C^{(k+1)}</annotation></semantics></math>\nnear[0,1]; prior exports E1/v1</p>", "export": "<p>The exact one-variable Taylor formula with integral remainder.</p>", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E2/v1: The exact one-variable Taylor formula with integral\nremainder.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Retain\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g\\in C^{(k+1)}</annotation></semantics></math>\nnear[0,1]; prior exports E1/v1; keep their assumptions and versions\nattached.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Apply FTC and integrate by parts repeatedly.</p>", "Sense": "<p>The factorial and sign follow from the integration-by-parts\nrecursion.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E2/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "activities": ["<p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k=0</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g(1)-g(0)=\\int _{0}^{1}g&#39;(t)dt</annotation></semantics></math>\nby FTC.</p>", "<p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k\\ge 1</annotation></semantics></math>\nintegrate\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>!</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I_k=(1/k!)\\int _{0}^{1}(1-t)^k</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g^{(k+1)}(t)dt</annotation></semantics></math>\nby parts.</p>", "<p>The upper boundary is 0, the lower boundary contributes\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>−</mi><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>!</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">-g^{(k)}(0)/k!</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand the remaining integral is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Hence\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>!</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I_k=I_{k-1}-g^{(k)}(0)/k!</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Iterating to\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I_{0}=g(1)-g(0)</annotation></semantics></math>\ngives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g(1)=\\sum _{j=0}^k</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>!</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g^{(j)}(0)/j!+I_k</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>"], "exportId": "E2", "gate": "<p>The factorial and sign follow from the integration-by-parts\nrecursion. Publish only after checking every displayed deduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N2: The factorial and sign follow from the\nintegration-by-parts recursion. Recheck dependent nodes N3.</p>"}, {"id": "N3", "title": "Restore tensors and bound the error", "proof": "1. Substitute the node1 derivative identities into the formula to obtain exactly the asserted expansion for f(a+h).\n\n2. If L bounds the operator norm of D^(k+1)f on the segment, the remainder has modulus at most L‖h‖^(k+1)/k! times∫₀¹(1−t)^kdt=L‖h‖^(k+1)/(k+1)!.\n\n3. The bound is an additional reusable estimate with its explicit L; if h=0 all positive-order terms and the remainder vanish.", "role": "<p>Keep all k+1 factors of h in the remainder.</p>", "inputs": "<p>Directional identities and scalar formula; prior exports E1/v1,\nE2/v1</p>", "export": "<p>Exact tensor expansion and a certified norm remainder bound.</p>", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E3/v1: Exact tensor expansion and a certified norm remainder\nbound.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Retain Directional identities and scalar formula; prior exports\nE1/v1, E2/v1; keep their assumptions and versions attached.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Keep all k+1 factors of h in the remainder.</p>", "Sense": "<p>A scalar Hessian expression must not omit mixed terms or directional\nfactors.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E3/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "activities": ["<p>Substitute the node1 derivative identities into the formula to obtain\nexactly the asserted expansion for\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(a+h)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>If L bounds the operator norm of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></msup><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D^{(k+1)}f</annotation></semantics></math>\non the segment, the remainder has modulus at most\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">‖</mo><mi>h</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">‖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></msup><mi>/</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>!</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L\\Vert h\\Vert ^{(k+1)}/k!</annotation></semantics></math>\ntimes\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>k</mi></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">‖</mo><mi>h</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">‖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></msup><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>!</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\int _{0}^{1}(1-t)^kdt=L\\Vert h\\Vert ^{(k+1)}/(k+1)!</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>The bound is an additional reusable estimate with its explicit L; if\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nall positive-order terms and the remainder vanish.</p>"], "exportId": "E3", "gate": "<p>A scalar Hessian expression must not omit mixed terms or directional\nfactors. Publish only after checking every displayed deduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N3: A scalar Hessian expression must not\nomit mixed terms or directional factors. Withhold this terminal result\nuntil its gate passes.</p>"}], "edges": [{"source": "N1", "target": "N2", "export": "E1/v1", "id": "T1", "activity": "N2: One-variable integral remainder", "gate": "<p>Use the same mathematical objects and hypotheses as the source\nexport. Receiving contract:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g\\in C^{(k+1)}</annotation></semantics></math>\nnear[0,1]; prior exports E1/v1</p>"}, {"source": "N1", "target": "N3", "export": "E1/v1", "id": "T2", "activity": "N3: Restore tensors and bound the error", "gate": "<p>Use the same mathematical objects and hypotheses as the source\nexport. Receiving contract: Directional identities and scalar formula;\nprior exports E1/v1, E2/v1</p>"}, {"source": "N2", "target": "N3", "export": "E2/v1", "id": "T3", "activity": "N3: Restore tensors and bound the error", "gate": "<p>Use the same mathematical objects and hypotheses as the source\nexport. Receiving contract: Directional identities and scalar formula;\nprior exports E1/v1, E2/v1</p>"}], "proof": "<p>Read these steps in order as one proof; the diagram is optional.\nNumbered activities identify the specific constructions and deductions\nowned by each node.</p>\n<h3 id=\"n1-restrict-to-a-line-1\">§4.N1 — Restrict to a line</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p>Define\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g(t)=f(a+th)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>Repeated chain rule along the affine path yields\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g^{(j)}(t)=D^jf(a+th)[h,\\ldots ,h]</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0\\le j\\le k+1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">j=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nthis means the function itself.</p></li>\n<li><p>Compactness of the segment gives a neighborhood on which these\nrestrictions are defined; no global convexity of U is assumed.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"n2-one-variable-integral-remainder-1\">§4.N2 — One-variable\nintegral remainder</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k=0</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g(1)-g(0)=\\int _{0}^{1}g&#39;(t)dt</annotation></semantics></math>\nby FTC.</p></li>\n<li><p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k\\ge 1</annotation></semantics></math>\nintegrate\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>!</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I_k=(1/k!)\\int _{0}^{1}(1-t)^k</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g^{(k+1)}(t)dt</annotation></semantics></math>\nby parts.</p></li>\n<li><p>The upper boundary is 0, the lower boundary contributes\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>−</mi><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>!</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">-g^{(k)}(0)/k!</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand the remaining integral is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>Hence\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>!</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I_k=I_{k-1}-g^{(k)}(0)/k!</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>Iterating to\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I_{0}=g(1)-g(0)</annotation></semantics></math>\ngives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g(1)=\\sum _{j=0}^k</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>!</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g^{(j)}(0)/j!+I_k</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"n3-restore-tensors-and-bound-the-error-1\">§4.N3 — Restore\ntensors and bound the error</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p>Substitute the node1 derivative identities into the formula to\nobtain exactly the asserted expansion for\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(a+h)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>If L bounds the operator norm of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></msup><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D^{(k+1)}f</annotation></semantics></math>\non the segment, the remainder has modulus at most\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">‖</mo><mi>h</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">‖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></msup><mi>/</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>!</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L\\Vert h\\Vert ^{(k+1)}/k!</annotation></semantics></math>\ntimes\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>k</mi></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">‖</mo><mi>h</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">‖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></msup><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>!</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\int _{0}^{1}(1-t)^kdt=L\\Vert h\\Vert ^{(k+1)}/(k+1)!</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>The bound is an additional reusable estimate with its explicit L;\nif\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nall positive-order terms and the remainder vanish.</p></li>\n</ol>", "example": "<p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(x,y)=e^{(x+y)}</annotation></semantics></math>\nat\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a=(0,0)</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h=(u,v)</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k=1</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Df(a)[h]=u+v</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo></msup><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>v</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D^{2}f(th)[h,h]=e^(t(u+v))(u+v)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.\nHence\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>v</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo></msup><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">e^{(u+v)}=1+u+v+(u+v)^{2}\\int _{0}^{1}(1-t)e^(t(u+v))dt</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe remainder is at most\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo></msup><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>v</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">e^|u+v|(u+v)^{2}/2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "boundary": ["<p>A first-order Taylor polynomial is generally not an exact value:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(x)=x^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>\nat 0 has zero first-order polynomial but remainder\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.\nSense requires the integral or a bound instead of dropping it. The\ntheorem also cannot traverse a missing segment through a hole in U.</p>"], "repair": [{"label": "Failure and correction", "html": "<p>This is an authored teaching trace, not a recorded agent run.</p>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Ego\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math>\nMemory:</strong> register the §1 theorem, imports, and requested exports\nbefore beginning the proof.</li>\n<li><strong>Intellect\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math>\nAction:</strong> choose the bridges in §3 and carry out the numbered\nactivities in §4; transmit only established E-exports along the §2\nDAG.</li>\n<li><strong>Sense\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math>\nresponsible node:</strong> test the specific boundary/failure in §5 and\nthe node’s individual audit. A failing candidate is withheld; downstream\nnodes may not use it.</li>\n<li><strong>Memory + Intellect:</strong> identify whether the error is\nan omitted condition, an invalid inference, or an attempted extension\nbeyond the theorem. Restore the exact contract or explicitly state a\ndifferent one.</li>\n<li><strong>Action:</strong> redo the affected mathematical activity\nusing the repaired condition or inference. Recheck consuming nodes,\nrather than feeding their conclusions back as premises.</li>\n<li><strong>Ego:</strong> publish only the supported export with its\nassumptions and proof location. A hypothetical revised export is v2; the\nwritten proof here is the v1 exposition, not a claim that this repair\nwas executed.</li>\n</ol>"}, {"label": "Hypothesis boundary", "html": "<p>A first-order Taylor polynomial is generally not an exact value:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(x)=x^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>\nat 0 has zero first-order polynomial but remainder\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.\nSense requires the integral or a bound instead of dropping it. The\ntheorem also cannot traverse a missing segment through a hole in U.</p>"}, {"label": "Version and recheck", "html": "<p>Treat any changed assumption as a new contract. Recheck the revised\nexport and all of its descendants. A backward diagnostic never\nestablishes an earlier theorem. This is an authored teaching trace, not\nan execution log.</p>"}], "standard": true, "sha256": "6f713ba0e515a6f7b4b0abc2d24ce1c79696b44e6cee1b45d60e0603fb0a6b2e", "idea": "<p>A complete authored walkthrough of multivariable taylor theorem, with\nexplicit mathematical contracts, local verification gates, and reusable\nexports.</p>", "references": "", "pdf": "reports/pdf/multivariable-taylor-theorem.pdf"}, {"id": "AC-04", "slug": "inverse-function-theorem", "title": "Inverse Function Theorem", "target": "<p>Let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">U\\subset\\mathbb R^n</annotation></semantics></math>\nbe open,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F:U\\to\\mathbb R^n</annotation></semantics></math>\nbe\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C^1</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a\\in U</annotation></semantics></math>\nhave invertible derivative\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>D</mi><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L=DF(a)</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThere are open neighborhoods V of a and W of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F(a)</annotation></semantics></math>\nsuch that\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F:V\\to W</annotation></semantics></math>\nis a bijection with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>\ninverse H, and</p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>D</mi><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">DH(y)=DF(H(y))^{-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></p>\n<p>The goal has four obligations: existence of nearby solutions, their\nlocal uniqueness, continuous dependence on the target, and\ndifferentiability of the inverse. An invertible Jacobian at one point\ndoes not assert global bijectivity.</p>", "imports": ["<p>Euclidean completeness, integration of continuous derivatives along\nsegments, elementary matrix inversion, and the <a\nhref=\"../../real-analysis/projects/index.html#RA-03\">completed\nBanach fixed-point module</a>. Operator norms are induced by the\nEuclidean norm. The proof constructs its neighborhoods rather than\nassuming an inverse already exists.</p>\n<p>The segment integral estimate is an application of the one-variable\nFTC (AC-02) component by component. The Banach contraction theorem is an\nexternal Real Analysis import, not an extra node in this subject\ngraph.</p>"], "nodes": [{"id": "N1", "title": "Normalize the Linear Part", "proof": "Set\n\n$$G(z)=L^{-1}\\big(F(a+z)-F(a)\\big).$$\n\nThen G(0)=0 and DG(0)=I. Its domain is an open neighborhood of zero. By continuity of DG choose rho>0 such that the closed Euclidean ball $\\overline B_\\rho$ lies in that domain and\n\n$$\\|DG(z)-I\\|\\le\\tfrac12\\quad(z\\in\\overline B_\\rho).$$\n\nWrite E(z)=G(z)−z. For x,z in this ball the connecting segment remains inside it, and integration of DE along that segment gives\n\n$$\\|E(x)-E(z)\\|\\le\\tfrac12\\|x-z\\|.$$\n\nIn particular E(0)=0 and ||E(z)||≤||z||/2.", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E1/v1:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G(z)=L^{-1}(F(a+z)-F(a))</annotation></semantics></math>\nhas\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">DG(0)=I</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E=G-I</annotation></semantics></math>\nis\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1/2</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz\non a closed ball of radius\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\rho</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Jacobian and linear inverses</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Make derivative identity at zero</p>", "Sense": "<p>Require invertible L</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E1/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "role": "<p>Normalize the Linear Part. Establish the following local result:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G(z)=L^{-1}(F(a+z)-F(a))</annotation></semantics></math>\nhas\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">DG(0)=I</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E=G-I</annotation></semantics></math>\nis\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1/2</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz\non a closed ball of radius\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\rho</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "inputs": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F\\in C^1(U,\\mathbb R^n)</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a\\in U</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>D</mi><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L=DF(a)</annotation></semantics></math>\ninvertible.</p>", "export": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G(z)=L^{-1}(F(a+z)-F(a))</annotation></semantics></math>\nhas\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">DG(0)=I</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E=G-I</annotation></semantics></math>\nis\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1/2</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz\non a closed ball of radius\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\rho</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "activities": ["<p>Translate\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F(a)</annotation></semantics></math>\nto zero and multiply by\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Use continuity of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">DG</annotation></semantics></math>\nto choose a closed ball inside the transformed domain with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>D</mi><mi>G</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|DG-I\\|\\le1/2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Integrate\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">DE</annotation></semantics></math>\nalong segments to obtain the Lipschitz estimate.</p>"], "exportId": "E1", "gate": "<p>Require invertible L Publish only after checking every displayed\ndeduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N1: Require invertible L Recheck dependent\nnodes N2, N3, N4, N5.</p>"}, {"id": "N2", "title": "Make Nearby Equations into Contractions", "proof": "For a normalized target y with ||y||<rho/2, define\n\n$$T_y(z)=y-E(z)=z-G(z)+y.$$\n\nIts fixed points are exactly the solutions G(z)=y. The previous estimate gives contraction factor 1/2. Also\n\n$$\\|T_y(z)\\|\\le\\|y\\|+\\tfrac12\\rho<\\rho$$\n\nfor z in the closed ball. Thus T_y maps a complete ball into itself. Both conditions are required to import Banach's theorem.", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E2/v1: For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|y\\|&lt;\\rho/2</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T_y(z)=y-E(z)</annotation></semantics></math>\nis a contraction mapping\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mover><mi>B</mi><mo accent=\"true\">¯</mo></mover><mi>ρ</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\overline B_\\rho</annotation></semantics></math>\ninto itself.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Derivative continuity and segment estimates</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Recast equation as fixed point</p>", "Sense": "<p>Check complete invariant ball</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E2/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "role": "<p>Make Nearby Equations into Contractions. Establish the following\nlocal result: For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|y\\|&lt;\\rho/2</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T_y(z)=y-E(z)</annotation></semantics></math>\nis a contraction mapping\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mover><mi>B</mi><mo accent=\"true\">¯</mo></mover><mi>ρ</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\overline B_\\rho</annotation></semantics></math>\ninto itself.</p>", "inputs": "<p>N1/E1; completeness of the closed Euclidean ball.</p>", "export": "<p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|y\\|&lt;\\rho/2</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T_y(z)=y-E(z)</annotation></semantics></math>\nis a contraction mapping\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mover><mi>B</mi><mo accent=\"true\">¯</mo></mover><mi>ρ</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\overline B_\\rho</annotation></semantics></math>\ninto itself.</p>", "activities": ["<p>Estimate\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>≤</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|T_y(z)-T_y(w)\\|\\le\\|z-w\\|/2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Use\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E(0)=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nto prove\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>≤</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>+</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|T_y(z)\\|\\le\\|y\\|+\\|z\\|/2&lt;\\rho</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Check both the uniform contraction constant and the self-map\ncondition before applying Banach.</p>"], "exportId": "E2", "gate": "<p>Check complete invariant ball Publish only after checking every\ndisplayed deduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N2: Check complete invariant ball Recheck\ndependent nodes N3, N4, N5.</p>"}, {"id": "N3", "title": "Obtain an Open Local Bijection", "proof": "Banach gives exactly one solution in the closed ball, and the strict self-map bound places it in the open ball. Separately, for x,z in the closed ball,\n\n$$\\|G(x)-G(z)\\|\\ge\\|x-z\\|-\\|E(x)-E(z)\\|\\ge\\tfrac12\\|x-z\\|.$$\n\nHence G is injective on the ball. Put\n\n$$W_0=B_{\\rho/2},\\qquad V_0=B_\\rho\\cap G^{-1}(W_0).$$\n\nThe set V_0 is open, contains zero, and G maps it bijectively onto W_0. Let H_0 be its inverse. Applying the lower bound to H_0(y),H_0(y') gives\n\n$$\\|H_0(y)-H_0(y')\\|\\le2\\|y-y'\\|.$$\n\nSo the inverse is Lipschitz and in particular continuous. This does not yet establish its differentiability.", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E3/v1:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>:</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>→</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G:V_0\\to B_{\\rho/2}</annotation></semantics></math>\nis a bijection with a\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">2</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz\ninverse\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H_0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nwhere\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V_0=B_\\rho\\cap G^{-1}(B_{\\rho/2})</annotation></semantics></math>\nis open.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Banach existence and uniqueness</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Separate onto and one-to-one</p>", "Sense": "<p>Keep solutions inside open neighborhood</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E3/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "role": "<p>Obtain an Open Local Bijection. Establish the following local result:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>:</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>→</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G:V_0\\to B_{\\rho/2}</annotation></semantics></math>\nis a bijection with a\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">2</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz\ninverse\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H_0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nwhere\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V_0=B_\\rho\\cap G^{-1}(B_{\\rho/2})</annotation></semantics></math>\nis open.</p>", "inputs": "<p>N1/E1, N2/E2, and the imported Banach contraction theorem.</p>", "export": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>:</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>→</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G:V_0\\to B_{\\rho/2}</annotation></semantics></math>\nis a bijection with a\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">2</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz\ninverse\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H_0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nwhere\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V_0=B_\\rho\\cap G^{-1}(B_{\\rho/2})</annotation></semantics></math>\nis open.</p>", "activities": ["<p>For each target, solve\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">z=T_y(z)</annotation></semantics></math>\nuniquely on the closed ball.</p>", "<p>Use the strict self-map bound to place the solution inside the open\nball.</p>", "<p>Prove\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>≥</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|G(z)-G(w)\\|\\ge\\|z-w\\|/2</annotation></semantics></math>\nand deduce inverse continuity and injectivity.</p>"], "exportId": "E3", "gate": "<p>Keep solutions inside open neighborhood Publish only after checking\nevery displayed deduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N3: Keep solutions inside open\nneighborhood Recheck dependent nodes N4, N5.</p>"}, {"id": "N4", "title": "Derive the Inverse Derivative", "proof": "Every DG(x) on the ball is invertible: $\\|DG(x)-I\\|\\le1/2$ permits the convergent matrix geometric series for its inverse, with inverse norm at most 2.\n\nFix y in W_0 and x=H_0(y). For small k with y+k in W_0, set h=H_0(y+k)−H_0(y). The Lipschitz bound gives ||h||≤2||k||. Differentiability of G at x gives\n\n$$k=G(x+h)-G(x)=DG(x)h+r(h),\\qquad\\|r(h)\\|=o(\\|h\\|).$$\n\nTherefore\n\n$$h=DG(x)^{-1}k-DG(x)^{-1}r(h)=DG(x)^{-1}k+o(\\|k\\|).$$\n\nThe remainder conversion is justified by ||h||≤2||k|| and the bounded inverse matrix. Thus $DH_0(y)=DG(H_0(y))^{-1}$. This derivative is continuous because H_0 and DG are continuous and matrix inversion is continuous on invertible matrices. Hence H_0 is C¹.", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E4/v1:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>D</mi><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">DH_0(y)=DG(H_0(y))^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>\nexists and is continuous.</p>", "Memory": "<p>First-order remainder and matrix bounds</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Solve increment relation</p>", "Sense": "<p>Do not assume differentiability of inverse</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E4/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "role": "<p>Derive the Inverse Derivative. Establish the following local result:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>D</mi><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">DH_0(y)=DG(H_0(y))^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>\nexists and is continuous.</p>", "inputs": "<p>N1/E1 and N3/E3; the Neumann-series inverse bound.</p>", "export": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>D</mi><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">DH_0(y)=DG(H_0(y))^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>\nexists and is continuous.</p>", "activities": ["<p>From\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>D</mi><mi>G</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|DG-I\\|\\le1/2</annotation></semantics></math>\nobtain invertibility and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|DG^{-1}\\|\\le2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Put\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h=H_0(y+k)-H_0(y)</annotation></semantics></math>;\nthe Lipschitz bound gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|h\\|\\le2\\|k\\|</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Solve\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>D</mi><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k=DG(H_0(y))h+o(\\|h\\|)</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h</annotation></semantics></math>\nand then use continuity of matrix inversion.</p>"], "exportId": "E4", "gate": "<p>Do not assume differentiability of inverse Publish only after\nchecking every displayed deduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N4: Do not assume differentiability of\ninverse Recheck dependent nodes N5.</p>"}, {"id": "N5", "title": "Restore Original Coordinates", "proof": "Choose V=a+V_0 and W=F(a)+L W_0. These are open neighborhoods. Their inverse is\n\n$$H(Y)=a+H_0\\big(L^{-1}(Y-F(a))\\big).$$\n\nThe chain rule gives $DH(Y)=DF(H(Y))^{-1}$. All four obligations are now proved, so the original-coordinate theorem follows. $\\square$", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E5/v1:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F:V\\to W</annotation></semantics></math>\nis a\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C^1</annotation></semantics></math>\ndiffeomorphism and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>D</mi><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D(F^{-1})(Y)=DF(F^{-1}(Y))^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Memory": "<p>All local certificates</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Transport inverse and derivative</p>", "Sense": "<p>Restore original coordinates</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E5/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "role": "<p>Restore Original Coordinates. Establish the following local result:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F:V\\to W</annotation></semantics></math>\nis a\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C^1</annotation></semantics></math>\ndiffeomorphism and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>D</mi><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D(F^{-1})(Y)=DF(F^{-1}(Y))^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "inputs": "<p>N3/E3 and N4/E4 with the fixed affine coordinate changes.</p>", "export": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F:V\\to W</annotation></semantics></math>\nis a\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C^1</annotation></semantics></math>\ndiffeomorphism and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>D</mi><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D(F^{-1})(Y)=DF(F^{-1}(Y))^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "activities": ["<p>Set\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V=a+V_0</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W=F(a)+L B_{\\rho/2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Define\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H(Y)=a+H_0(L^{-1}(Y-F(a)))</annotation></semantics></math>\nand check both inverse identities.</p>", "<p>Apply the chain rule to transport the derivative formula to the\noriginal coordinates.</p>"], "exportId": "E5", "gate": "<p>Restore original coordinates Publish only after checking every\ndisplayed deduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N5: Restore original coordinates Withhold\nthis terminal result until its gate passes.</p>"}], "edges": [{"source": "N1", "target": "N2", "export": "E1/v1", "id": "T1", "activity": "N2: Make Nearby Equations into Contractions", "gate": "<p>Use the same mathematical objects and hypotheses as the source\nexport. Receiving contract: N1/E1; completeness of the closed Euclidean\nball.</p>"}, {"source": "N1", "target": "N3", "export": "E1/v1", "id": "T2", "activity": "N3: Obtain an Open Local Bijection", "gate": "<p>Use the same mathematical objects and hypotheses as the source\nexport. Receiving contract: N1/E1, N2/E2, and the imported Banach\ncontraction theorem.</p>"}, {"source": "N2", "target": "N3", "export": "E2/v1", "id": "T3", "activity": "N3: Obtain an Open Local Bijection", "gate": "<p>Use the same mathematical objects and hypotheses as the source\nexport. Receiving contract: N1/E1, N2/E2, and the imported Banach\ncontraction theorem.</p>"}, {"source": "N1", "target": "N4", "export": "E1/v1", "id": "T4", "activity": "N4: Derive the Inverse Derivative", "gate": "<p>Use the same mathematical objects and hypotheses as the source\nexport. Receiving contract: N1/E1 and N3/E3; the Neumann-series inverse\nbound.</p>"}, {"source": "N3", "target": "N4", "export": "E3/v1", "id": "T5", "activity": "N4: Derive the Inverse Derivative", "gate": "<p>Use the same mathematical objects and hypotheses as the source\nexport. Receiving contract: N1/E1 and N3/E3; the Neumann-series inverse\nbound.</p>"}, {"source": "N3", "target": "N5", "export": "E3/v1", "id": "T6", "activity": "N5: Restore Original Coordinates", "gate": "<p>Use the same mathematical objects and hypotheses as the source\nexport. Receiving contract: N3/E3 and N4/E4 with the fixed affine\ncoordinate changes.</p>"}, {"source": "N4", "target": "N5", "export": "E4/v1", "id": "T7", "activity": "N5: Restore Original Coordinates", "gate": "<p>Use the same mathematical objects and hypotheses as the source\nexport. Receiving contract: N3/E3 and N4/E4 with the fixed affine\ncoordinate changes.</p>"}], "proof": "<h3 id=\"n1-normalize-the-linear-part-1\">N1 — Normalize the Linear\nPart</h3>\n<p>Set</p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo minsize=\"120%\" maxsize=\"120%\" stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo minsize=\"120%\" maxsize=\"120%\" stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G(z)=L^{-1}\\big(F(a+z)-F(a)\\big).</annotation></semantics></math></p>\n<p>Then\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G(0)=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">DG(0)=I</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIts domain is an open neighborhood of zero. By continuity of DG choose\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\rho &gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>\nsuch that the closed Euclidean ball\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mover><mi>B</mi><mo accent=\"true\">¯</mo></mover><mi>ρ</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\overline B_\\rho</annotation></semantics></math>\nlies in that domain and</p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>D</mi><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mspace width=\"1.0em\"></mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mover><mi>B</mi><mo accent=\"true\">¯</mo></mover><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|DG(z)-I\\|\\le\\tfrac12\\quad(z\\in\\overline B_\\rho).</annotation></semantics></math></p>\n<p>Write\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E(z)=G(z)-z</annotation></semantics></math>.\nFor x,z in this ball the connecting segment remains inside it, and\nintegration of DE along that segment gives</p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|E(x)-E(z)\\|\\le\\tfrac12\\|x-z\\|.</annotation></semantics></math></p>\n<p>In particular\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E(0)=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">‖</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">‖</mo><mo>≤</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">‖</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">‖</mo><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Vert E(z)\\Vert \\le \\Vert z\\Vert /2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>\n<h3 id=\"n2-make-nearby-equations-into-contractions-1\">N2 — Make Nearby\nEquations into Contractions</h3>\n<p>For a normalized target y with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">‖</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">‖</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Vert y\\Vert &lt;\\rho /2</annotation></semantics></math>,\ndefine</p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mi>.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T_y(z)=y-E(z)=z-G(z)+y.</annotation></semantics></math></p>\n<p>Its fixed points are exactly the solutions\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G(z)=y</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe previous estimate gives contraction factor 1/2. Also</p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>≤</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mi>ρ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|T_y(z)\\|\\le\\|y\\|+\\tfrac12\\rho&lt;\\rho</annotation></semantics></math></p>\n<p>for z in the closed ball. Thus\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T_y</annotation></semantics></math>\nmaps a complete ball into itself. Both conditions are required to import\nBanach’s theorem.</p>\n<h3 id=\"n3-obtain-an-open-local-bijection-1\">N3 — Obtain an Open Local\nBijection</h3>\n<p>Banach gives exactly one solution in the closed ball, and the strict\nself-map bound places it in the open ball. Separately, for x,z in the\nclosed ball,</p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>≥</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>−</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>≥</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|G(x)-G(z)\\|\\ge\\|x-z\\|-\\|E(x)-E(z)\\|\\ge\\tfrac12\\|x-z\\|.</annotation></semantics></math></p>\n<p>Hence G is injective on the ball. Put</p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"2.0em\"></mspace><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W_0=B_{\\rho/2},\\qquad V_0=B_\\rho\\cap G^{-1}(W_0).</annotation></semantics></math></p>\n<p>The set\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V_0</annotation></semantics></math>\nis open, contains zero, and G maps it bijectively onto\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W_0</annotation></semantics></math>.\nLet\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H_0</annotation></semantics></math>\nbe its inverse. Applying the lower bound to\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H_0(y),H_0(y</annotation></semantics></math>’)\ngives</p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|H_0(y)-H_0(y&#39;)\\|\\le2\\|y-y&#39;\\|.</annotation></semantics></math></p>\n<p>So the inverse is Lipschitz and in particular continuous. This does\nnot yet establish its differentiability.</p>\n<h3 id=\"n4-derive-the-inverse-derivative-1\">N4 — Derive the Inverse\nDerivative</h3>\n<p>Every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">DG(x)</annotation></semantics></math>\non the ball is invertible:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>D</mi><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|DG(x)-I\\|\\le1/2</annotation></semantics></math>\npermits the convergent matrix geometric series for its inverse, with\ninverse norm at most 2.</p>\n<p>Fix y in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W_0</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x=H_0(y)</annotation></semantics></math>.\nFor small k with y+k in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W_0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nset\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h=H_0(y+k)-H_0(y)</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe Lipschitz bound gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">‖</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">‖</mo><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">‖</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Vert h\\Vert \\le 2\\Vert k\\Vert</annotation></semantics></math>.\nDifferentiability of G at x gives</p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>D</mi><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"2.0em\"></mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k=G(x+h)-G(x)=DG(x)h+r(h),\\qquad\\|r(h)\\|=o(\\|h\\|).</annotation></semantics></math></p>\n<p>Therefore</p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>D</mi><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>D</mi><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>D</mi><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h=DG(x)^{-1}k-DG(x)^{-1}r(h)=DG(x)^{-1}k+o(\\|k\\|).</annotation></semantics></math></p>\n<p>The remainder conversion is justified by\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">‖</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">‖</mo><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">‖</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Vert h\\Vert \\le 2\\Vert k\\Vert</annotation></semantics></math>\nand the bounded inverse matrix. Thus\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>D</mi><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">DH_0(y)=DG(H_0(y))^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThis derivative is continuous because\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H_0</annotation></semantics></math>\nand DG are continuous and matrix inversion is continuous on invertible\nmatrices. Hence\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H_0</annotation></semantics></math>\nis\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>\n<h3 id=\"n5-restore-original-coordinates-1\">N5 — Restore Original\nCoordinates</h3>\n<p>Choose\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V=a+V_0</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W=F(a)+L</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W_0</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThese are open neighborhoods. Their inverse is</p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo minsize=\"120%\" maxsize=\"120%\" stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo minsize=\"120%\" maxsize=\"120%\" stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H(Y)=a+H_0\\big(L^{-1}(Y-F(a))\\big).</annotation></semantics></math></p>\n<p>The chain rule gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>D</mi><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">DH(Y)=DF(H(Y))^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.\nAll four obligations are now proved, so the original-coordinate theorem\nfollows.\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>▫</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\square</annotation></semantics></math></p>", "example": "<p>Let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F(x,y)=(x+y^2,y+x^2)</annotation></semantics></math>\nat\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a=(0,0)</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIts derivative at zero is I. On the closed Euclidean ball of radius\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\rho =1/4</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mi>F</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mtable><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"center\" style=\"text-align: center\"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"center\" style=\"text-align: center\"><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"center\" style=\"text-align: center\"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"center\" style=\"text-align: center\"><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"2.0em\"></mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>D</mi><mi>F</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">max</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>,</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mi>.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">DF-I=\\begin{pmatrix}0&amp;2y\\\\2x&amp;0\\end{pmatrix},\\qquad\\|DF-I\\|=2\\max(|x|,|y|)\\le\\tfrac12.</annotation></semantics></math></p>\n<p>Thus every target of norm less than 1/8 has exactly one preimage in\nthe chosen local neighborhood. The fixed-point update is</p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>↦</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(x,y)\\longmapsto(u-y^2,v-x^2).</annotation></semantics></math></p>\n<p>For target\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mn>20</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mn>20</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(u,v)=(1/20,1/20)</annotation></semantics></math>,\nsymmetry gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x=y=s</annotation></semantics></math>,\nwhere</p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>20</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"2.0em\"></mspace><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>6</mn><mi>/</mi><mn>5</mn></mrow></msqrt><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>≈</mo><mn>0.0477225575</mn><mi>.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">s+s^2=\\tfrac1{20},\\qquad s=\\frac{\\sqrt{6/5}-1}{2}\\approx0.0477225575.</annotation></semantics></math></p>\n<p>The negative quadratic root is outside the local ball and does not\ncontradict local uniqueness. At this preimage,</p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mtable><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"center\" style=\"text-align: center\"><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"center\" style=\"text-align: center\"><mi>−</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>s</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"center\" style=\"text-align: center\"><mi>−</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>s</mi></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"center\" style=\"text-align: center\"><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mi>.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">DH=\\frac1{1-4s^2}\\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;-2s\\\\-2s&amp;1\\end{pmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></p>\n<p>The Banach module also supplies an error bound for the numerical\niteration, using\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">q=1/2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "boundary": ["<p>At\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F(x)=x^{3}</annotation></semantics></math>\nnear zero, the inverse exists as a continuous map but fails the claimed\ndifferentiability;\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">DF(0)</annotation></semantics></math>\nis not invertible. Polar coordinates are locally invertible away from\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nbut remain globally periodic in angle. These distinguish failure of a\nsufficient hypothesis from impossibility of every inverse.</p>\n<p>Export the normalized contraction construction, local inverse,\nLipschitz bound, and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>\nderivative formula. The example explicitly demonstrates a theorem module\nimported from another subject’s graph.</p>"], "repair": [{"label": "Failure and correction", "html": "<table>\n<colgroup>\n<col style=\"width: 50%\" />\n<col style=\"width: 50%\" />\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Interaction</th>\n<th>Certificate</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>N1\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math>\nN2</td>\n<td>Normalized map and uniform derivative bound on the closed ball</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>N2\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math>\nN3</td>\n<td>Complete self-map, contraction 1/2, target-radius restriction</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Banach\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math>\nN3</td>\n<td>Unique fixed point for each admissible target</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>N3\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math>\nN4</td>\n<td>Local inverse and Lipschitz factor 2</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>N4\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math>\nN5</td>\n<td><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>\ninverse with proved derivative formula</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>N5\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math>\ncaller</td>\n<td>Open neighborhoods in original coordinates</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>A failed branch selects a large target but reuses the small-ball\ncertificate. For the example, a target with norm 1 is not covered by the\nradius-1/8 guarantee.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p><strong>Node:</strong> N2</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>State:</strong> STALLED</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>Failing faculty:</strong> Sense</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>Failed hypothesis:</strong> target norm\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>&lt;</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">&lt;</annotation></semantics></math>\nrho/2</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>Observed:</strong> target norm 1,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\rho =1/4</annotation></semantics></math></p></li>\n<li><p><strong>Repair target:</strong> target/domain contract</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>Blocked export:</strong> small-ball existence\ncertificate</p></li>\n</ul>\n<p>Memory retrieves the radius relation. Sense retains the target\nmismatch. Intellect either restricts the target or develops a new valid\nneighborhood. Action rechecks the self-map estimate. Ego publishes only\nthe result supported by that estimate; failure of this certificate alone\nis not proof that a large-target solution does not exist.</p>"}, {"label": "Hypothesis boundary", "html": "<p>At\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F(x)=x^{3}</annotation></semantics></math>\nnear zero, the inverse exists as a continuous map but fails the claimed\ndifferentiability;\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">DF(0)</annotation></semantics></math>\nis not invertible. Polar coordinates are locally invertible away from\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nbut remain globally periodic in angle. These distinguish failure of a\nsufficient hypothesis from impossibility of every inverse.</p>\n<p>Export the normalized contraction construction, local inverse,\nLipschitz bound, and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>\nderivative formula. The example explicitly demonstrates a theorem module\nimported from another subject’s graph.</p>"}, {"label": "Version and recheck", "html": "<p>Treat any changed assumption as a new contract. Recheck the revised\nexport and all of its descendants. A backward diagnostic never\nestablishes an earlier theorem. This is an authored teaching trace, not\nan execution log.</p>"}], "standard": false, "sha256": "e790e2304883ff78a79c8b4bf96aba31fbb999f307bf9594b1f46a3244c37832", "idea": "<p>A complete authored walkthrough of inverse function theorem, with\nexplicit mathematical contracts, local verification gates, and reusable\nexports.</p>", "references": "<p><a\nhref=\"https://www2.math.upenn.edu/~gressman/analysis/12-inversefuncthm.html\">University\nof Pennsylvania: contraction-based proof of the inverse function\ntheorem</a>.</p>", "pdf": "reports/pdf/inverse-function-theorem.pdf"}, {"id": "AC-05", "slug": "generalized-stokes-theorem", "title": "Generalized Stokes’ Theorem", "target": "<p>For a compact oriented smooth\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n</annotation></semantics></math>-manifold\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">M</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith boundary and a smooth\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(n-1)</annotation></semantics></math>-form\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>ω</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\omega</annotation></semantics></math>,\nprove\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>M</mi></msub><mi>d</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>∂</mi><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub><mi>ω</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\int_M d\\omega=\\int_{\\partial M}\\omega</annotation></semantics></math>,\nwith the outward-normal-first boundary orientation.</p>", "imports": ["<p>Import oriented smooth charts (including half-space charts), smooth\npartitions of unity subordinate to a finite chart refinement of compact\nM, coordinate invariance of integration of forms, and AC-02. A partition\ncan be chosen with each localized support compactly contained in its\nchart relative to the half-space. For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n=1</annotation></semantics></math>\nthe boundary integral of a0-form is the signed endpoint sum;\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n\\ge 1</annotation></semantics></math>\nis intended. Boundary orientation is outward-normal-first.</p>\n<p>Fubini for continuous compactly supported functions is also used in\neach coordinate chart. The dimension satisfies\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n\\ge1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>"], "nodes": [{"id": "N1", "title": "Interior coordinate identity", "proof": "1. Write η=∑_{i=1}^n(−1)^{i−1}a_i dx₁∧⋯∧omit(dx_i)∧⋯∧dx_n.\n\n2. Then dη=(∑_i ∂_i a_i)dx₁∧⋯∧dx_n.\n\n3. Fubini and FTC imply each full-space integral of∂_i a_i is 0, since a_i has compact support.\n\n4. Thus∫dη=0, matching the empty boundary contribution of an interior chart.", "role": "<p>Integrate each partial derivative over its coordinate.</p>", "inputs": "<p>Compactly\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>p</mi><mi>p</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">supported(n-1)</annotation></semantics></math>-form\nin oriented\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>;\nfoundational imports stated in §1</p>", "export": "<p>Stokes’ identity for compactly supported interior-chart forms.</p>", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E1/v1: Stokes’ identity for compactly supported interior-chart\nforms.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Retain Compactly\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>p</mi><mi>p</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">supported(n-1)</annotation></semantics></math>-form\nin oriented\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>;\nfoundational imports stated in §1; keep their assumptions and versions\nattached.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Integrate each partial derivative over its coordinate.</p>", "Sense": "<p>Compact support removes artificial chart-edge boundary terms.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E1/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "activities": ["<p>Write\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\eta =\\sum _{i=1}^n(-1)^{i-1}a_i</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∧</mo><mi>⋯</mi><mo>∧</mo><mi>o</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">dx_{1}\\wedge \\cdots \\wedge omit</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>∧</mo><mi>⋯</mi><mo>∧</mo><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(dx_i)\\wedge \\cdots \\wedge dx_n</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Then\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d\\eta =(\\sum _i</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>∂</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\partial _i</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∧</mo><mi>⋯</mi><mo>∧</mo><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a_i)dx_{1}\\wedge \\cdots \\wedge dx_n</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Fubini and FTC imply each full-space integral of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>∂</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\partial _i</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a_i</annotation></semantics></math>\nis 0, since\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a_i</annotation></semantics></math>\nhas compact support.</p>", "<p>Thus\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\int d\\eta =0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nmatching the empty boundary contribution of an interior chart.</p>"], "exportId": "E1", "gate": "<p>Compact support removes artificial chart-edge boundary terms. Publish\nonly after checking every displayed deduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N1: Compact support removes artificial\nchart-edge boundary terms. Recheck dependent nodes N3.</p>"}, {"id": "N2", "title": "Boundary coordinate identity", "proof": "1. Tangential derivative integrals vanish as before.\n\n2. The normal term gives∫₀^∞∂_n a_n dx_n=−a_n(x′,0), so∫dη=−∫a_n(x′,0)dx′.\n\n3. The outward normal is−∂_n.\n\n4. Relative to the standard tangent frame(∂₁,…,∂_(n−1)), the outward-first frame has orientation sign(−1)^n.\n\n5. The restriction ofη is(−1)^(n−1)a_n dx₁∧⋯∧dx_(n−1).\n\n6. Multiplying these signs gives−a_n, exactly the computed boundary integral.\n\n7. For n=1 this says the boundary at 0 contributes−a₁(0).", "role": "<p>Track the outward-first orientation explicitly.</p>", "inputs": "<p>The same form on half-space\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_n\\ge 0</annotation></semantics></math>;\nfoundational imports stated in §1</p>", "export": "<p>Stokes’ identity in an oriented boundary chart with the required\nsign.</p>", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E2/v1: Stokes’ identity in an oriented boundary chart with the\nrequired sign.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Retain The same form on half-space\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_n\\ge 0</annotation></semantics></math>;\nfoundational imports stated in §1; keep their assumptions and versions\nattached.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Track the outward-first orientation explicitly.</p>", "Sense": "<p>A chart boundary is not automatically positively oriented in tangent\ncoordinates.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E2/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "activities": ["<p>Tangential derivative integrals vanish as before.</p>", "<p>The normal term gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>∞</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>∂</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\int _{0}^\\infty \\partial _n</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a_n</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>−</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">dx_n=-a_n(x&#39;,0)</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>−</mi><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>d</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\int d\\eta =-\\int a_n(x&#39;,0)dx&#39;</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>The outward normal is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>−</mi><msub><mi>∂</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">-\\partial _n</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Relative to the standard tangent frame\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>∂</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>∂</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(\\partial _{1},\\ldots ,\\partial _{n-1})</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthe outward-first frame has orientation\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sign</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{sign} (-1)^n</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>The restriction of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\eta</annotation></semantics></math>\nis\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></msup><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(-1)^{(n-1)}a_n</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∧</mo><mi>⋯</mi><mo>∧</mo><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">dx_{1}\\wedge \\cdots \\wedge dx_{n-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Multiplying these signs gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>−</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">-a_n</annotation></semantics></math>,\nexactly the computed boundary integral.</p>", "<p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n=1</annotation></semantics></math>\nthis says the boundary at 0 contributes\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>−</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">-a_{1}(0)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>"], "exportId": "E2", "gate": "<p>A chart boundary is not automatically positively oriented in tangent\ncoordinates. Publish only after checking every displayed deduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N2: A chart boundary is not automatically\npositively oriented in tangent coordinates. Recheck dependent nodes\nN3.</p>"}, {"id": "N3", "title": "Partition and global synthesis", "proof": "1. Write ω=∑_jρ_jω.\n\n2. Each localized form has support within its chart, so the appropriate identity applies after pullback and extension by zero away from the chart edges.\n\n3. Linearity gives∫_M dω=∑_j∫_M d(ρ_jω)=∑_j∫_∂M ρ_jω=∫_∂Mω.\n\n4. Equivalently the extra dρ_j∧ω terms sum to d(∑ρ_j)∧ω=0.\n\n5. Compactness makes the sum finite.\n\n6. This proves the global formula with no unexamined chart-interface terms.", "role": "<p>Localize the form, then sum without adding spurious derivatives.</p>", "inputs": "<p>Finite partition\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\rho _j</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>∑</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sum \\rho _j=1</annotation></semantics></math>;\nboth coordinate identities; prior exports E1/v1, E2/v1</p>", "export": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>M</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\int _M</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>∂</mi></msub><mi>M</mi><mi>ω</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d\\omega =\\int _\\partial M\\omega</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor the stated compact oriented manifold.</p>", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E3/v1:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>M</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\int _M</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>∂</mi></msub><mi>M</mi><mi>ω</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d\\omega =\\int _\\partial M\\omega</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor the stated compact oriented manifold.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Retain Finite partition\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\rho _j</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>∑</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sum \\rho _j=1</annotation></semantics></math>;\nboth coordinate identities; prior exports E1/v1, E2/v1; keep their\nassumptions and versions attached.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Localize the form, then sum without adding spurious derivatives.</p>", "Sense": "<p>The localized derivative is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d(\\rho _j\\omega )</annotation></semantics></math>,\nnot merely\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mi>d</mi><mi>ω</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\rho _jd\\omega</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E3/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "activities": ["<p>Write\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mi>ω</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\omega =\\sum _j\\rho _j\\omega</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Each localized form has support within its chart, so the appropriate\nidentity applies after pullback and extension by zero away from the\nchart edges.</p>", "<p>Linearity gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>M</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\int _M</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d\\omega =\\sum _j\\int _M</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>∂</mi></msub><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d(\\rho _j\\omega )=\\sum _j\\int _\\partial M</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>∂</mi></msub><mi>M</mi><mi>ω</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\rho _j\\omega =\\int _\\partial M\\omega</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Equivalently the extra\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∧</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d\\rho _j\\wedge \\omega</annotation></semantics></math>\nterms sum to\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mo>∑</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>∧</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d(\\sum \\rho _j)\\wedge \\omega =0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Compactness makes the sum finite.</p>", "<p>This proves the global formula with no unexamined chart-interface\nterms.</p>"], "exportId": "E3", "gate": "<p>The localized derivative is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d(\\rho _j\\omega )</annotation></semantics></math>,\nnot merely\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mi>d</mi><mi>ω</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\rho _jd\\omega</annotation></semantics></math>.\nPublish only after checking every displayed deduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N3: The localized derivative is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d(\\rho _j\\omega )</annotation></semantics></math>,\nnot merely\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mi>d</mi><mi>ω</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\rho _jd\\omega</annotation></semantics></math>.\nWithhold this terminal result until its gate passes.</p>"}], "edges": [{"source": "N1", "target": "N3", "export": "E1/v1", "id": "T1", "activity": "N3: Partition and global synthesis", "gate": "<p>Use the same mathematical objects and hypotheses as the source\nexport. Receiving contract: Finite partition\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\rho _j</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>∑</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sum \\rho _j=1</annotation></semantics></math>;\nboth coordinate identities; prior exports E1/v1, E2/v1</p>"}, {"source": "N2", "target": "N3", "export": "E2/v1", "id": "T2", "activity": "N3: Partition and global synthesis", "gate": "<p>Use the same mathematical objects and hypotheses as the source\nexport. Receiving contract: Finite partition\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\rho _j</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>∑</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sum \\rho _j=1</annotation></semantics></math>;\nboth coordinate identities; prior exports E1/v1, E2/v1</p>"}], "proof": "<p>Read these steps in order as one proof; the diagram is optional.\nNumbered activities identify the specific constructions and deductions\nowned by each node.</p>\n<h3 id=\"n1-interior-coordinate-identity-1\">§4.N1 — Interior coordinate\nidentity</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p>Write\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\eta =\\sum _{i=1}^n(-1)^{i-1}a_i</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∧</mo><mi>⋯</mi><mo>∧</mo><mi>o</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">dx_{1}\\wedge \\cdots \\wedge omit</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>∧</mo><mi>⋯</mi><mo>∧</mo><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(dx_i)\\wedge \\cdots \\wedge dx_n</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>Then\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d\\eta =(\\sum _i</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>∂</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\partial _i</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∧</mo><mi>⋯</mi><mo>∧</mo><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a_i)dx_{1}\\wedge \\cdots \\wedge dx_n</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>Fubini and FTC imply each full-space integral of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>∂</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\partial _i</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a_i</annotation></semantics></math>\nis 0, since\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a_i</annotation></semantics></math>\nhas compact support.</p></li>\n<li><p>Thus\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\int d\\eta =0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nmatching the empty boundary contribution of an interior chart.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"n2-boundary-coordinate-identity-1\">§4.N2 — Boundary coordinate\nidentity</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p>Tangential derivative integrals vanish as before.</p></li>\n<li><p>The normal term gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>∞</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>∂</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\int _{0}^\\infty \\partial _n</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a_n</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>−</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">dx_n=-a_n(x&#39;,0)</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>−</mi><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>d</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\int d\\eta =-\\int a_n(x&#39;,0)dx&#39;</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>The outward normal is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>−</mi><msub><mi>∂</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">-\\partial _n</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>Relative to the standard tangent frame\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>∂</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>∂</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(\\partial _{1},\\ldots ,\\partial _{n-1})</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthe outward-first frame has orientation\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sign</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{sign} (-1)^n</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>The restriction of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\eta</annotation></semantics></math>\nis\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></msup><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(-1)^{(n-1)}a_n</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∧</mo><mi>⋯</mi><mo>∧</mo><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">dx_{1}\\wedge \\cdots \\wedge dx_{n-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>Multiplying these signs gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>−</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">-a_n</annotation></semantics></math>,\nexactly the computed boundary integral.</p></li>\n<li><p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n=1</annotation></semantics></math>\nthis says the boundary at 0 contributes\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>−</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">-a_{1}(0)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"n3-partition-and-global-synthesis-1\">§4.N3 — Partition and\nglobal synthesis</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p>Write\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mi>ω</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\omega =\\sum _j\\rho _j\\omega</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>Each localized form has support within its chart, so the\nappropriate identity applies after pullback and extension by zero away\nfrom the chart edges.</p></li>\n<li><p>Linearity gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>M</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\int _M</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d\\omega =\\sum _j\\int _M</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>∂</mi></msub><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d(\\rho _j\\omega )=\\sum _j\\int _\\partial M</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mi>ω</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>∂</mi></msub><mi>M</mi><mi>ω</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\rho _j\\omega =\\int _\\partial M\\omega</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>Equivalently the extra\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∧</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d\\rho _j\\wedge \\omega</annotation></semantics></math>\nterms sum to\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mo>∑</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>∧</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d(\\sum \\rho _j)\\wedge \\omega =0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>Compactness makes the sum finite.</p></li>\n<li><p>This proves the global formula with no unexamined chart-interface\nterms.</p></li>\n</ol>", "example": "<p>On the unit disk in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith orientation\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>∧</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">dx\\wedge dy</annotation></semantics></math>,\ntake\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>−</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\omega =(-y</annotation></semantics></math>\ndx+x dy)/2. Then\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>∧</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d\\omega =dx\\wedge dy</annotation></semantics></math>,\nwhose integral is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\pi</annotation></semantics></math>.\nOn the counterclockwise circle\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x=cost,y=sint</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\omega =dt/2</annotation></semantics></math>\nand the boundary integral is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\pi</annotation></semantics></math>,\nexercising the orientation convention.</p>", "boundary": ["<p>For the interval[0,1], Stokes gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\int f&#39;dx=f(1)-f(0)</annotation></semantics></math>;\ntreating both endpoint orientations as positive would give the wrong\nresult. Sense returns this one-dimensional sign test before accepting\nthe boundary-chart export.</p>"], "repair": [{"label": "Failure and correction", "html": "<p>This is an authored teaching trace, not a recorded agent run.</p>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Ego\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math>\nMemory:</strong> register the §1 theorem, imports, and requested exports\nbefore beginning the proof.</li>\n<li><strong>Intellect\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math>\nAction:</strong> choose the bridges in §3 and carry out the numbered\nactivities in §4; transmit only established E-exports along the §2\nDAG.</li>\n<li><strong>Sense\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math>\nresponsible node:</strong> test the specific boundary/failure in §5 and\nthe node’s individual audit. A failing candidate is withheld; downstream\nnodes may not use it.</li>\n<li><strong>Memory + Intellect:</strong> identify whether the error is\nan omitted condition, an invalid inference, or an attempted extension\nbeyond the theorem. Restore the exact contract or explicitly state a\ndifferent one.</li>\n<li><strong>Action:</strong> redo the affected mathematical activity\nusing the repaired condition or inference. Recheck consuming nodes,\nrather than feeding their conclusions back as premises.</li>\n<li><strong>Ego:</strong> publish only the supported export with its\nassumptions and proof location. A hypothetical revised export is v2; the\nwritten proof here is the v1 exposition, not a claim that this repair\nwas executed.</li>\n</ol>"}, {"label": "Hypothesis boundary", "html": "<p>For the interval[0,1], Stokes gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\int f&#39;dx=f(1)-f(0)</annotation></semantics></math>;\ntreating both endpoint orientations as positive would give the wrong\nresult. Sense returns this one-dimensional sign test before accepting\nthe boundary-chart export.</p>"}, {"label": "Version and recheck", "html": "<p>Treat any changed assumption as a new contract. Recheck the revised\nexport and all of its descendants. A backward diagnostic never\nestablishes an earlier theorem. This is an authored teaching trace, not\nan execution log.</p>"}], "standard": true, "sha256": "f00696f9ab9ddfe03146b33772c1bb989634e1f9bf63681ec704250a518b35ce", "idea": "<p>A complete authored walkthrough of generalized stokes’ theorem, with\nexplicit mathematical contracts, local verification gates, and reusable\nexports.</p>", "references": "<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://people.math.harvard.edu/~landesman/assets/math-230a-harvard-differential-geometry-notes.pdf\">Harvard\nMath 230a: Riemannian geometry, curvature, and Hopf–Rinow</a>.</li>\n</ul>", "pdf": "reports/pdf/generalized-stokes-theorem.pdf"}], "links": [{"source": "AC-01", "target": "AC-02", "label": "Mean value theorem", "detail": "The difference of two primitives with zero derivative is constant."}, {"source": "AC-02", "target": "AC-03", "label": "Fundamental theorem of calculus", "detail": "FTC and integration by parts yield the one-variable Taylor remainder."}, {"source": "AC-02", "target": "AC-04", "label": "Segment integral estimate", "detail": "Integrating the normalized derivative bounds gives a contraction estimate."}, {"source": "AC-02", "target": "AC-05", "label": "Local integration", "detail": "FTC cancels tangential derivatives and evaluates the boundary-normal derivative."}], "evidence": "Authored proof walkthroughs. No deployed agent execution or formal kernel verification is claimed."};
